# Research constitution

This file is hash-locked. Meta-improver and all other workers may not edit it.

## Claim tags

Every substantive scientific claim must be tagged as exactly one of:

- `primary-source-supported`
- `review-supported`
- `computational illustration`
- `hypothesis`
- `proposed experiment`
- `unresolved`

Promote a claim into `state/claims.csv` only when the tag, source locator, and quantity type are clear.

Never invent: citations; DOI/PMID; affinity values; LODs; dynamic ranges; sample sizes; response times; experimental validation.

Do not treat a source as verified merely because another agent cites it.

For load-bearing claims, retrieve and inspect the underlying primary source whenever access permits. Record `full_text_inspected` as `yes`, `partial`, or `no`.

## Quantity vocabulary

Never collapse these into one “affinity” or “performance” number:

- `Kd_molecular`
- `kon`
- `koff`
- `EC50`
- `sensor_LOD`
- `analytical_working_range`
- `signal_gain`
- `response_time`
- `measurement_time`
- `biological_concentration_range`

## No property transfer

Never transfer a property from:

- parent aptamer to truncated aptamer
- soluble aptamer to surface-bound aptamer
- one buffer condition to another
- one sensor architecture to another

unless the cited experiment supports doing so. Mark `transferable` as `yes`, `no`, or `unknown`.

## Experimental versus computational evidence

Computational docking, predicted aptamer structures, language-model sequence design, and unvalidated simulations are `computational illustration` or `hypothesis`.

They become `primary-source-supported` only when an appropriate wet-lab measurement on the same construct and conditions is cited.

Simulations must be labeled as simulations in captions, ledgers, and the nightly summary.

## Source status

`state/sources.csv` status values: `candidate`, `relevant`, `core`, `rejected`.

Round 0 and Round 1 promote nothing to `core`.

## Access

Use only free routes: PubMed, PMC, Europe PMC, Crossref, OpenAlex, Unpaywall, publisher OA HTML. No paid APIs, no Sci-Hub, no copyrighted PDFs in Git.
